## Early Warning Joe objectives, batch 2 (ARCH-02 withdrawal and reroll, ARCH-03 new directives).

# ARCH-02: stale directives and the player's reroll
cmu-ew-joe-objective-withdrawn-stale = A directive can no longer be fulfilled. The signal withdraws it; another will come.
cmu-ew-joe-reroll-done = The signal hears your request. A new directive replaces the old.
cmu-ew-joe-reroll-not-ready = The signal will not hear another request yet.
cmu-ew-joe-reroll-refused = That directive cannot be exchanged.
cmu-ew-joe-reroll-none = The signal has nothing else to ask of you here. The directive stands.
cmu-ew-joe-status-reroll-ready = REQUEST CHANNEL :: OPEN (one directive may be exchanged)
cmu-ew-joe-status-reroll-spent = REQUEST CHANNEL :: CLOSED
cmu-ew-joe-status-reroll-button = Request new directive

# N3 Tithe of Flesh-Work
cmu-ew-joe-objective-collect-flesh-work-title = Tithe of Flesh-Work: take {$count} robotic limbs.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-collect-flesh-work-description = Take {$count} robotic limbs or hands into your hands or onto your frame, from the colony or from those who wear them. Your own frame does not count. Each counts once; you need not keep it.

# N4 Offer the Ordnance
cmu-ew-joe-objective-offer-ordnance-title = Offer the Ordnance: {$count} explosives.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-offer-ordnance-description = Find {$count} grenades or other explosives lying loose in the colony and Offer them to the Grand Machine. What is offered is gone for good.

# N5 Blind the Watch (ARCH-11: a Meld directive)
cmu-ew-joe-objective-blind-watch-title = Blind the Watch: meld {$count} cameras.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-blind-watch-description = Offer {$count} of the colony's security cameras to the Grand Machine. Each is melded into the river where it hangs: it glows with the river's light and watches no more, unless someone burns the meld out with a welder.

# N6 Silence the Colony (ARCH-11: a Meld directive)
cmu-ew-joe-objective-silence-colony-title = Silence the Colony: meld {$count} telecomms servers.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-silence-colony-description = Offer {$count} of the colony's telecommunications servers to the Grand Machine. Each is melded into the river where it stands: it glows with the river's light and carries no voice, unless someone burns the meld out with a welder.

# N7 Darken a District
cmu-ew-joe-objective-darken-district-title = Darken a District: {$area}.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-darken-district-description = Black out {$area} with your own hands, by striking the APC, reactor or generator that feeds it, and keep it dark for {$minutes} minutes. A darkness you did not make does not count.
cmu-ew-joe-darken-dark = {$area} falls dark by your hand. Keep it so.
cmu-ew-joe-darken-relit = The light returns to {$area}. Darken it again.
cmu-ew-joe-darken-not-yours = The district fell dark without you.
cmu-ew-joe-darken-repinned = The signal turns your eyes to {$area} instead.
cmu-ew-joe-darken-exhausted = No lit district remains to darken.

# N9 Purge the Nest
cmu-ew-joe-objective-purge-nest-title = Purge {$count} of the xenofauna's works.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-purge-nest-description = Offer what the planet's xenofauna has built or grown to the Grand Machine: its walls, its eggs, its nests. A nest counts for more. Its cores are beyond the offering. What is offered is gone for good.

# ARCH-11: an Offer that melds a structure instead of taking it in
cmu-ew-joe-offer-melded = {CAPITALIZE($item)} is melded into the river. Its light turns to the Grand Machine's.

# N11 Bear Witness
cmu-ew-joe-objective-bear-witness-title = Bear Witness: judge {$count} souls.
cmu-ew-joe-objective-bear-witness-description = Let {$count} different people meet the signal's gaze through your Test of Faith or Judgement. Each casting counts no more than two.

# RB-30: a welder burns the river's meld out of a camera or telecomms server
cmu-ew-joe-meld-repair-start = You start burning the strange orange glow out of {THE($target)}.
cmu-ew-joe-meld-repair-done = The orange glow fades from {THE($target)}. It works again.
